   At the end of this workflow, the user will have a fully prepared, solvated, and ionised GROMACS system for the ATP‑bound q9y243 protein, with two distinct TPR files for independent simulation replicates. No simulation execution has taken place; only the preprocessing and setup stages have been completed, producing the following deliverables in the analysis folder:
   
   - `protein_h.pdb` (cleaned protein with hydrogens)  
   - `ligand_h.pdb` (cleaned ligand with hydrogens)  
   - `ligand.itp` (ligand topology)  
   - `system.top` (full system topology)  
   - `system.gro` (coordinate file)  
   - `system.mdp` (simulation parameters)  
   - `rep1.tpr` (first replicate starting file)  
   - `rep2.tpr` (second replicate starting file)  
   
   These files constitute a ready‑to‑run simulation setup that adheres to the user’s specifications and the pipeline constraints.
